1
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:53,020
[The Old Story of Yu Hong]

2
00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:55,900
[Episode 30]

3
00:00:57,740 --> 00:00:59,400
Why isn't the baby coming yet?

4
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:02,980
Don't even mention it. When I had my son,

5
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:04,900
I was in labor for over 20 hours—

6
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:05,810
a whole night.

7
00:01:08,590 --> 00:01:10,000
Where's that bread?

8
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:11,900
Let me have a bite
so I don't run out of energy later.

9
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:12,570
You hungry?

10
00:01:12,570 --> 00:01:13,789
Here, eat up.

11
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:15,289
Here. Take it away.

12
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:16,760
Don't eat that. It's too dry.

13
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:17,210
That's better.

14
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:17,680
Have some noodles.

15
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:18,060
Noodles?

16
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:18,900
-With chicken soup.
-This is good.

17
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:19,780
Chicken noodle soup.

18
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,730
Let me sit up a bit.

19
00:01:20,730 --> 00:01:21,460
Take it easy.

20
00:01:24,460 --> 00:01:25,720
Prop yourself up a bit.

21
00:01:31,210 --> 00:01:32,200
My phone.

22
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,930
Okay, don't worry about it.

23
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:34,560
My phone.

24
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:38,680
Hello?

25
00:01:38,820 --> 00:01:39,820
Where's Ms. Chen?

26
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:40,810
Ms. Chen is in the hospital.

27
00:01:40,810 --> 00:01:41,870
What's up? Tell me.

28
00:01:42,039 --> 00:01:42,930
Are you okay?

29
00:01:43,979 --> 00:01:45,670
The order hasn't been placed.

30
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:47,410
It hasn't been signed yet.

31
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,289
Then place it.

32
00:01:48,289 --> 00:01:49,400
Why are you waiting for a signature?

33
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,009
Just do it normally.

34
00:01:50,009 --> 00:01:52,009
Find that... that procurement guy.

35
00:01:52,310 --> 00:01:53,090
Hold on.

36
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:57,380
Hello? Get that order placed right away.

37
00:01:57,479 --> 00:01:58,850
Bring the purchase order to the hospital.

38
00:01:58,850 --> 00:01:59,460
I'll sign it first.

39
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,520
Ship the goods as soon as it's signed.

40
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,770
Let's do both things at once, okay?

41
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:07,070
I used to only see this kind of

42
00:02:07,070 --> 00:02:08,530
strong woman on TV.

43
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:10,199
Today I've seen a real one.

44
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:12,090
Good thing I'm smart.

45
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:14,050
I was really good at math in school.

46
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:15,600
As soon as I joined the factory,

47
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,260
I started working in finance.

48
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:19,440
Your business—

49
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:21,690
it's not like some small street shop.

50
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:23,960
It's not enough to just
be good with numbers.

51
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,050
I think you've

52
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:26,800
got this drive.

53
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,280
Really sharp.

54
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:30,260
If you were in ancient times,

55
00:02:30,710 --> 00:02:32,230
you'd be Wu Zetian.

56
00:02:33,390 --> 00:02:36,170
Juan, please, don't make fun of me.

57
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:37,880
What Wu Zetian?

58
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,910
Only the people
in this factory listen to me.

59
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:41,150
No one else does.

60
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:43,470
A whole factory of people needs to be fed.

61
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:45,840
Do you know how hard
it is to get business now?

62
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,960
I ran around with a big belly
for two whole months.

63
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:48,970
You know the Hong Kong businessmen

64
00:02:48,970 --> 00:02:50,470
coming for investment and renovation?

65
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:51,730
I just landed one deal,

66
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,930
signed the contract,

67
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:54,410
and this little one's about to come out.

68
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:56,210
Isn't that a hassle? Seriously.

69
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:57,560
Listen to me.

70
00:02:58,090 --> 00:02:59,020
You have to do your

71
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:00,750
postpartum recovery properly,

72
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:02,480
or you'll end up with problems.

73
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:04,210
Yuhong Square is right under my nose.

74
00:03:04,210 --> 00:03:07,010
If anything comes up,
I'll keep an eye on it for you.

75
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:09,010
Okay, Juan. Sorry to trouble you.

76
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,540
No, I can't eat anymore.

77
00:03:10,540 --> 00:03:12,130
Still feeling uncomfortable?

78
00:03:12,130 --> 00:03:13,460
It's pushing up to here.

79
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:14,190
Why is

80
00:03:14,190 --> 00:03:15,960
this kid so patient?

81
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,620
Why aren't you coming out yet?

82
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:18,530
If you don't come out soon,

83
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:19,250
I'm going back to the station.

84
00:03:19,250 --> 00:03:20,190
Come here, let me lean on you a bit.

85
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:21,579
You have no idea. Recently,

86
00:03:21,579 --> 00:03:23,380
that renovation project you just mentioned

87
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:24,390
has worn us out.

88
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:25,430
We've been rushed off our feet.

89
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:26,079
Why?

90
00:03:26,670 --> 00:03:28,000
A few old neighborhoods

91
00:03:28,150 --> 00:03:30,079
need to be demolished and cleared.

92
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,250
Siying Road,

93
00:03:31,550 --> 00:03:32,420
Labor Park—

94
00:03:32,450 --> 00:03:34,170
that whole area is under our jurisdiction.

95
00:03:34,170 --> 00:03:35,170
All the officers at the station

96
00:03:35,170 --> 00:03:37,100
are working day and night
checking records.

97
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:38,100
We're exhausted.

98
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,579
It's a mess over there.

99
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,840
We are helping the investor

100
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:44,030
check the previous residents and handle

101
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:45,630
the demolition procedures.

102
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:47,650
That area is not small.

103
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,690
Searching like that—how long will it take?

104
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:52,670
Tell me about it.

105
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:54,210
From last month until now,

106
00:03:54,210 --> 00:03:54,930
we've only reached

107
00:03:54,930 --> 00:03:56,030
less than a third.

108
00:03:57,630 --> 00:03:59,140
What if they don't live there anymore?

109
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:00,020
What then?

110
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:00,930
What can we do?

111
00:04:00,930 --> 00:04:02,300
We contact their families

112
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:03,560
and their workplaces.

113
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,210
Anyway, no matter what,

114
00:04:04,210 --> 00:04:05,750
we have to get all the procedures done

115
00:04:05,750 --> 00:04:07,210
before they can demolish.

116
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:09,740
Feeling uncomfortable, aren't you?

117
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:11,340
Yeah, it's stuck right here.

118
00:04:11,690 --> 00:04:13,490
No, you still need to sit up a bit.

119
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:18,029
Still no good. I'm uncomfortable.

120
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,450
Who's it?

121
00:04:19,930 --> 00:04:21,260
What are you looking at?

122
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:23,390
She's smiling at you.

123
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:25,220
She's making me laugh, staring at me.

124
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,480
Look at this forehead.

125
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:28,720
She'd be smart with the big forehead.

126
00:04:29,510 --> 00:04:31,100
So pretty.

127
00:04:32,159 --> 00:04:33,130
Your little head is out.

128
00:04:33,130 --> 00:04:34,530
She wants you to hold her.

129
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:35,570
Let me hold her.

130
00:04:35,570 --> 00:04:36,540
Support her head with one hand.

131
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:38,670
And support her bottom with the other.

132
00:04:40,270 --> 00:04:41,280
Little head.

133
00:04:42,270 --> 00:04:43,400
Support the bottom.

134
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:44,560
Who's it?

135
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,920
Who's it? Who's so pretty?

136
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:50,240
This little nose and little mouth.

137
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,610
This baby smell.

138
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,690
Your eyes look like your mom's.

139
00:04:54,770 --> 00:04:56,500
You'll definitely be a little beauty
when you grow up.

140
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,100
Let me hold your little head.

141
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:00,750
Good girl.

142
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:01,330
Yes.

143
00:05:01,330 --> 00:05:02,720
Hold her like this?

144
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,420
Yes.

145
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:04,130
Nice and smooth.

146
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:05,570
Who's it? What are you looking at?

147
00:05:05,570 --> 00:05:07,950
Whose little face is so pretty?

148
00:05:09,710 --> 00:05:10,420
No, no.

149
00:05:10,450 --> 00:05:11,950
Hurry, Liu Yang.

150
00:05:11,950 --> 00:05:12,810
Help me out. Come.

151
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:14,100
Hurry. Help me.

152
00:05:14,930 --> 00:05:16,280
Support her.

153
00:05:17,140 --> 00:05:18,710
Catch her little head.

154
00:05:19,010 --> 00:05:19,580
Careful.

155
00:05:19,630 --> 00:05:21,310
Still likes being with Daddy,

156
00:05:21,310 --> 00:05:21,980
huh?

157
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:25,390
Little thing.

158
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:31,620
My former mother-in-law

159
00:05:32,110 --> 00:05:33,480
used to force me to have a baby.

160
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,030
She told me a child

161
00:05:35,190 --> 00:05:36,790
is a gift from God.

162
00:05:37,190 --> 00:05:37,920
I told her

163
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,610
we cops don't accept gifts.

164
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,810
Now I don't know if it's because
I'm getting older or what,

165
00:05:43,810 --> 00:05:45,250
but I really like kids.

166
00:06:47,850 --> 00:06:50,400
[Honest Business, Serving the People]

167
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:52,060
[Shasha Hair Salon]

168
00:06:52,090 --> 00:06:55,210
[Sealed, Yuhong Square Demolition Office,
Tieqiao District, Tiecheng City]

169
00:07:01,190 --> 00:07:02,340
We're closed.

170
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:14,660
It's you.

171
00:07:15,570 --> 00:07:16,420
Hair wash?

172
00:07:18,130 --> 00:07:19,250
Can I still get one?

173
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:24,030
Sure.

174
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:57,659
Come in.

175
00:08:18,690 --> 00:08:20,150
When are you closing down?

176
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:23,980
It was supposed to be
the end of the month.

177
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:27,730
But there's been no business
these past couple days.

178
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:30,980
So I figured I'd start packing up.

179
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,429
Just these couple days.

180
00:08:36,630 --> 00:08:37,960
So what'll you do after?

181
00:08:39,549 --> 00:08:41,150
I'm not getting any younger.

182
00:08:43,289 --> 00:08:44,620
I think I'll have a baby.

183
00:08:49,010 --> 00:08:49,910
That's good.

184
00:08:57,790 --> 00:08:59,290
After we both got laid off,

185
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,590
I opened this shop.

186
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:07,220
If I could've made a living any other way,

187
00:09:08,300 --> 00:09:10,630
I wouldn't have done this shady business.

188
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:15,240
I know.

189
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:17,250
People look down on me.

190
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:19,790
Well, if it's getting
demolished, so be it.

191
00:09:19,790 --> 00:09:21,520
We'll open a restaurant later.

192
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,660
We're both good cooks.

193
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:27,150
It might be hard,

194
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:29,580
but at least

195
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:32,080
we can be together.

196
00:09:35,520 --> 00:09:37,480
So I won't have to lie awake

197
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:40,400
worrying every time he drives at night.

198
00:09:58,550 --> 00:09:59,620
Later,

199
00:10:01,050 --> 00:10:02,580
when the restaurant opens,

200
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:06,400
you have to come and try it.

201
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:09,990
My fried pork is really delicious.

202
00:10:16,210 --> 00:10:17,670
I just love fried pork.

203
00:10:20,010 --> 00:10:22,340
My mom used to make it for me
when I was a kid.

204
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:25,170
Then she got senile,

205
00:10:25,670 --> 00:10:27,330
so I stopped letting her cook.

206
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:30,380
Afraid she'd set the kitchen on fire.

207
00:10:34,620 --> 00:10:36,480
My sister likes vegetarian food.

208
00:10:37,790 --> 00:10:39,820
I haven't had fried pork in years.

209
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:42,490
I'll make it for you.

210
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:45,480
All you can eat.

211
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:52,890
By the way,

212
00:11:02,240 --> 00:11:03,270
the card

213
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:06,040
you topped up here last time

214
00:11:06,530 --> 00:11:08,130
still has a lot of money left.

215
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:11,290
But I didn't bring enough today.

216
00:11:11,940 --> 00:11:13,650
I'll go to the bank tomorrow

217
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:15,170
and give it to you later.

218
00:11:15,170 --> 00:11:16,170
Count this first.

219
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:25,020
Just consider it a prepaid card.

220
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:28,990
When your restaurant opens,

221
00:11:29,370 --> 00:11:31,500
I'll definitely eat my money's worth.

222
00:11:34,670 --> 00:11:35,360
Alright.

223
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:38,650
Then leave me your pager number.

224
00:11:40,130 --> 00:11:40,870
When it opens,

225
00:11:40,870 --> 00:11:42,400
you'll be the first to know.

226
00:14:35,670 --> 00:14:36,530
Let me know as soon

227
00:14:36,530 --> 00:14:37,930
as you sign the contract.

228
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:38,790
Without my approval,

229
00:14:38,790 --> 00:14:39,750
do not ship anything.

230
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:40,480
You hear me?

231
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:43,740
What's wrong?

232
00:14:52,170 --> 00:14:53,250
You're awake.

233
00:14:53,250 --> 00:14:54,510
I'm going out for a bit.

234
00:14:55,030 --> 00:14:56,160
Where are you going?

235
00:15:01,130 --> 00:15:02,240
Mom.

236
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:03,720
Mom.

237
00:16:17,440 --> 00:16:18,450
[Jie, the money I sent you
last time got returned.]

238
00:16:18,480 --> 00:16:19,710
[Not sure why.
Did you change your address?]

239
00:16:19,730 --> 00:16:21,060
[Don't be afraid to spend money.
I'm a lobby manager now.]

240
00:16:21,090 --> 00:16:22,470
[I'm making good money.
Did you get scheduled for surgery?]

241
00:16:22,490 --> 00:16:23,230
[Let me know when it is.
I'll take leave and go to Shanghai.]

242
00:16:23,250 --> 00:16:24,310
[Mom's doing well at the nursing home.
Don't worry.]

243
00:16:32,220 --> 00:16:33,090
[Jie, the money I sent you
last time got returned.]

244
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,250
[Not sure why.
Did you change your address?]

245
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,250
[Golden Imperial Dance Hall]

246
00:17:21,270 --> 00:17:22,670
[Hao Peng, Golden Imperial Dance Hall
Entertainment Co., Ltd.]
